    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Partner Buggy are delighted to bring this beautifully presented, fully renovated and modernised bungalow to the market. Set in a peaceful countryside location, just 2 minutes from the picturesque village of Coon in North Kilkenny.\r\n\r\nThis charming turnkey property offers the perfect blend of modern comfort, character and exceptional outdoor space. Set on a generous site with beautifully maintained gardens, several useful outbuildings and two separate patio areas designed to make the most of the sunshine, this home is sure to appeal to garden enthusiasts, first-time buyers and young families alike. \r\n\r\nThe large private yard provides ample parking and plenty of outdoor space, while the mature, lovingly maintained gardens create a wonderful sense of peace and privacy.\r\n\r\nInside\r\nInternally, this immaculate home has been thoughtfully upgraded and is ready for immediate occupation. A beautiful parquet floor flows seamlessly throughout the accommodation, complemented by modern interior doors, shuttered windows and recessed lighting, creating a stylish yet warm and welcoming atmosphere.\r\n\r\nThe bright and spacious living/dining room provides an inviting hub for everyday family life and entertaining, with an attractive fireplace and mantle forming the focal point, complete with an insert electric stove.\r\n\r\nThe modern fitted kitchen offers excellent storage and is equipped with an integrated oven and ceramic hob, along with a fridge freezer, providing a practical and contemporary space for preparing and enjoying meals.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises three beautifully presented bedrooms, each offering built-in wardrobe space, while the fully tiled family bathroom completes the ground-floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nOutdoor Space\r\nOne of the property's standout features is undoubtedly its exceptional outdoor space. The beautifully maintained gardens offer a wonderful variety of areas to relax, entertain and enjoy the surrounding countryside. For someone who enjoys gardening, this could be a major attraction, while families would also have considerable space for children and outdoor activities.\r\n\r\nTwo separate patio areas maximise the sunshine throughout the day, while the selection of outbuildings provides excellent additional storage and potential for a variety of uses.\r\n\r\nThe generous yard offers substantial off-street parking and plenty of space for family life, gardening or outdoor hobbies.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nCoon is a small and picturesque rural village in north-east County Kilkenny, nestled in a peaceful valley close to the border with County Carlow.\r\n\r\nThe property is ideally positioned just 2 minutes (approximately 1.7km) from Coon village, where local amenities include Coon Church, St. Brigid's National School and St. Martin's GAA clubhouse and grounds.\r\n\r\nThe bustling market town of Castlecomer is approximately 12 minutes' drive (10km) away and offers a wide range of everyday amenities, including shops, cafés, takeaways, DIY stores, pubs, pharmacy. Castlecomer is also home to the renowned Castlecomer Discovery Park and Avalon House Hotel.\r\n\r\nFor commuters and those wishing to enjoy the amenities of larger towns and cities, Kilkenny City and Carlow town are both approximately 25 minutes' drive (21km) from the property.\r\n\r\nA Wonderful Country Home\r\nWith its turnkey condition, generous outdoor space, beautifully maintained gardens and convenient location, this delightful bungalow offers a rare opportunity to acquire a modernised country home with genuine charm and character.\r\n\r\nWhether you're looking for a peaceful family home, a property with exceptional garden space or simply somewhere to enjoy the best of rural living while remaining within easy reach of Kilkenny and Carlow, this property is sure to impress.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended through our office."
      },
      {
